A||N||5||stimpy||Why won't my car start today?||||5||
Z||000000||stimpy||08-01-2001||09:51 PM||||OK, I'm getting kinda tense here. In the past 6 months I have replaced my alternator, battery, and distributor cap. Everything else is less then 2 years old (complete rebuild). The car has usually had no problem firing up with a quick twist of the key. When I left work, it fired up reliably. However, when I went to go pick up Chinese for dinner an hour after I got home, it would crank like crazy, but wouldn't fire.  <BR>Factors to consider...<BR>1. It is hotter then hell's brass doorknob today, about 105 degrees.<P>2. The alternator has already needed to be replaced once due to not charging, and the volt gauge on the dash still reads BARELY 12 volts when the AC is on.<P>3.  After 3 trips back to the shop to have the belt tightened, it still squeals like a beat puppy. The belt may just be toast by now.<P>Any, all, or none of these may be factors. But any input from others would be most appreciated.<P>Help me Mr. Wizard!<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||sqoach||08-01-2001||10:22 PM||||I think the easiest solution would be to give your car to me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>On a serious note, I don't really think the heat is causing your problem. Mine has been starting just fine. Since you had your alternator replaced and you're showing low volts, you might have a loose wire or bad ground. I'm not sure how many times it takes to get the belt tight, but 3 times seems like it would be enough. Your pully's might be mis-aligned just a bit, causing the belt squeal, and that also might be killing your alternator. Man, I kinda sounded like I knew what I was talking about. Anyway, I hope someone else has some ideas for you.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">   <P>84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||08-01-2001||10:26 PM||||Doh! Double post.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-01-2001||11:39 PM||||the heat added to engine heat could have killed the distributor module, they can die in a second. mine did without warning. also load test your battery, my van battery died the other day with no warning too. even new alternator wouldnt charge it.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||JayUSA77||08-02-2001||12:16 AM||||if it cranks like a mad bi1ch then it cant be the battery or altenator. it might be ignition module, those go out often.<BR>J||||reg||1
